        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 04:06:20.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 73a-75e",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 73a-75e\n\nsanity-ec degraded-read subtests 73a-75e hard-coded an EC 4+2\nlayout with a gate of 6 or 8 OSTs, although the geometry did not\nmatter to what they tested.  They would be skipped on the 4 OST\ntest sessions, and 73x also on the 7 OST sessions.\n\nUse the EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec()\nscales to OSTCOUNT and drop the gates, so they run with 3 OSTs.\n75b and 75e write one row of EC_DSTRIPE stripes per file, and 75e\nchecks for EC_CSTRIPE parity stripes.  With only one parity stripe,\n73d and 73e skip their two-OST part.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Icde35ecd386787a74b40519a22c2ceec263ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
